  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Fan Tan (Sevens). Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Fan Tan, also widely known as 'Sevens', 'Domino', or 'Parliament', is a classic layout-based card game where the objective is to be the first to get rid of all your cards. Players build upon a central layout of cards, starting with the Sevens and expanding outward to the Ace and Two in each suit. It is a game of both luck and light strategy, as players can choose to hold back key 'blocking' cards to prevent opponents from playing.",
    objective: 'Find valid sets among the visible cards faster than the other players.',
    gameplay: 'Cards display combinations of colored dots. A tableau is exposed and players race to identify groups satisfying the projective-set rule. Correct calls claim cards or points; mistaken calls may be penalized by local rules.',
    keyRules: [
      'The deck contains every non-empty combination of six binary attributes.',
      'Players search the shared tableau in real time.',
      'A valid set follows the finite-geometry relationship defined by the card attributes.',
    ],
